@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry a ds:Subcomponent;
    ds:name "QueryChip.Entry";
    ds:summary "The part of a query chip being typed or edited: a text input inside the chip, where its field, operator or value is chosen. A chip holds at most one. When a part is settled, the host replaces the Entry with a Segment, or moves it to the next part.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "---\n# TODO implementation: no reference in @canonical/react-ds-global or react-ds-global-form\n# The part being typed: a native <input>, never a <textarea>, which admits no combobox\n# role. It renders only once scripts run, takes role=\"combobox\", and reads QueryInput's\n# suggestions through QueryInput's context. It has its own look, an input fill with an\n# underline, so the chip needs no editing state. The chip's body draws the focus ring\n# around the clause.\nnode:\n  uri: global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry\n  styles:\n    layout.type: inline-flex\n    layout.align: center\n    layout.position: relative\n    size.min.width: 4ch\n    size.min.height: dimension.300\n    spacing.internal.inline.start: 0.375rem\n    spacing.internal.inline.end: 0.375rem\n    appearance.background: [surface.color.foreground.input, color.foreground.input]\n    # @disabled is drawn from the chip's data attribute while the chip is disabled.\n    appearance.background@disabled: color.foreground.input.disabled\n    appearance.border.style: solid\n    appearance.border.width: 0\n    appearance.border.bottom.width: dimension.stroke.thickness.medium\n    appearance.border.bottom.color: color.border.highlighted\n    appearance.border.bottom.color@invalid: color.border.error\n    typography.font: typography.text.secondary\n    typography.color: color.text\n    typography.color@disabled: color.text.disabled\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        # The remaining props reach it.\n        role: entry input\n        styles:\n          layout.flex.grow: 1\n          size.min.width: 1ch\n          appearance.native: none\n          appearance.border.style: none\n          appearance.background: transparent\n          appearance.outline.style: none\n          typography.font: typography.text.secondary\n          typography.color: inherit\n          spacing.internal.block.start: 0\n          spacing.internal.block.end: 0\n          spacing.internal.inline.start: 0\n          spacing.internal.inline.end: 0\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              # Drawn as ::placeholder.\n              role: placeholder\n              styles:\n                typography.color: color.text.muted\n            relation:\n              cardinality: \"0..1\"\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"1\"\n    - node:\n        # An aria-hidden template behind the typed text: YYYY-MM-DD, or a range. The muted\n        # text symbol keeps the untyped part above 4.5:1.\n        role: format template\n        styles:\n          layout.position: absolute\n          interaction.pointerEvents: none\n          typography.whiteSpace: pre\n          typography.color: color.text.muted\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n    - node:\n        # Text after the typed text, such as a unit (\"GiB\"), from `suffix`.\n        role: suffix\n        styles:\n          typography.color: color.text.muted\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n    - node:\n        # The `formatDescription`, as a `hidden` element with an id, which the input's\n        # aria-describedby points at first and still resolves.\n        role: format description\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"\n    - node:\n        # The `description` while invalid, as a `hidden` element with an id, which the input's\n        # aria-describedby points at after the format description.\n        role: description\n      relation:\n        cardinality: \"0..1\"";
    ds:anatomyClassic "";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n- Inside a QueryChip, for the one part being typed: the next part of a draft chip, or the part  \nbeing edited.\n\n### When not to use\n\n- For a settled part: use **QueryChip.Segment**.\n- For free text, or the field of a new clause: that is **QueryInput**’s own entry.\n- On its own: use **TextInput** or **ComboboxInput**.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n- The Entry is a native `<input>`, never a `<textarea>`, which admits no combobox role. A long  \nvalue scrolls inside the input rather than wrapping.\n- It renders only once scripts run. It takes `role=\"combobox\"` and is named by `label`, such as  \n“Value for status”. It reads QueryInput’s suggestions through QueryInput’s context, and while  \nit has focus it carries `aria-controls`, `aria-expanded` and `aria-activedescendant` for  \nQueryInput’s listbox. It keeps focus while an option is highlighted.\n- Inside a roving composite, the Entry is its chip’s toolbar item while it is present, as  \n`<id>:entry`, and takes `tabindex=\"0\"` only while it holds the tab stop.\n- Its accessible description is always its `formatDescription`, when given, followed while  \ninvalid by its `description`, and, while QueryInput’s suggestions are open and carry a  \n`footer`, by that footer, which QueryInput supplies through its context. While invalid it  \nalso carries `aria-invalid`.\n- A format template is hidden from assistive technology; `formatDescription` says the format  \nin words.\n- Typing is never blocked by key filtering, so paste, dictation and input methods work. The  \nhost parses what was typed.\n\n### States & interaction\n\nThe Entry is default, focused, invalid, or disabled when its chip is disabled. It has its own  \nlook, an input fill with an underline, so the chip shows no editing state. While invalid it  \nshows the error underline; it takes no error fill and no glyph. Keys the combobox does not  \nhandle reach the host, which owns moving between parts and chips. Blur ends an edit only when  \nfocus leaves QueryInput’s root, a `focusout` whose `relatedTarget` is outside it.";
    ds:tier ds:global_dataviews;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.needstriage;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "value";
        ds:summary "The typed text.";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "on_value_change";
        ds:summary "Called with the typed text after each input.";
        ds:propertyType "callback";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "label";
        ds:summary "The accessible name, such as \"Value for status\".";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "placeholder";
        ds:summary "Shown while nothing is typed.";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "template";
        ds:summary "```A format template shown behind the typed text, such as `YYYY-MM-DD`.```";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "format_description";
        ds:summary "```The format in words, such as \"Date, format YYYY-MM-DD\", from the host's messages. It is always in the accessible description, before `description` while invalid.```";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "true";
        ds:constraints "```required with `template````"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "suffix";
        ds:summary "```Text after the typed text, such as a unit, as TextInput's `suffix` is.```";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "is_invalid";
        ds:summary "Marks the typed text invalid.";
        ds:propertyType "boolean";
        ds:optional "true";
        ds:constraints "```requires `description````";
        ds:defaultValue "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "description";
        ds:summary "The message, such as \"Invalid: <message>\".";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "true";
        ds:constraints "```required with `is_invalid````"
    ];
    ds:parentComponent ds:global_dataviews.component.query_chip;
    ds:hasTokenBinding [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "size.min.height";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.300
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.background";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:surface.color.foreground.input
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.background";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 2;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.foreground.input
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.background";
        anatomy:styleState "disabled";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.foreground.input.disabled
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.border.bottom.width";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:dimension.stroke.thickness.medium
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.border.bottom.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.border.highlighted
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "appearance.border.bottom.color";
        anatomy:styleState "invalid";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.border.error
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.font";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:typography.text.secondary
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.color";
        anatomy:styleState "disabled";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text.disabled
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root/entry input";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.font";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:typography.text.secondary
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root/entry input/placeholder";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text.muted
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root/format template";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text.muted
    ], [
        a ds:TokenBinding;
        ds:viaBlock ds:global_dataviews.subcomponent.query_chip-entry;
        ds:node "$root/suffix";
        anatomy:styleKey "typography.color";
        anatomy:styleState "default";
        ds:rank 1;
        ds:consumesSymbol dt:color.text.muted
    ].
